<%#
  Redirect.

  Shared by the domain page and the subdomain page, because a subdomain is
  just another website to Hestia and the question is identical: send everyone
  who visits this name somewhere else.

  People buy a second domain to hold the .co.uk beside the .com, to move to a
  new name, or to grab a misspelling; they make a subdomain to park `old.` or
  point `shop.` at a marketplace. All of it ends in "point it at the other
  site", which had no button and became a support ticket.

  THE FORM DOES NOT LEAD WITH "301". That number is the thing customers get
  wrong, and getting it wrong is expensive in a way nothing else on this
  page is: a permanent redirect is cached by the browser, sometimes until
  its cache is cleared, so a mistake follows that visitor around long after
  we have fixed the server. So the choice is worded as what it does, the
  consequence is spelled out under each option, and the number is shown for
  the people who came looking for it.
%>
<div class="p-card">
  <div class="row-between mb-2">
    <h2 class="h3">Redirect</h2>
    <% if (site && site.redirect) { %>
      <span class="badge badge-amber">On</span>
    <% } %>
  </div>

  <% if (!site) { %>
    <p class="small muted mb-0">
      <% if (!hasHosting) { %>
        There is no hosting on this account yet, so there is no website to redirect.
        <a href="/hosting">See the plans</a>.
      <% } else { %>
        This domain does not have a website on our server yet — point it at us first,
        using the panel on the right, and this appears.
      <% } %>
    </p>
  <% } else if (site.redirect) { %>
    <p class="small mb-3">
      Everyone visiting <b><%= domain.domain %></b> is sent to
      <b class="mono"><%= site.redirect %></b><%
        %><% if (site.redirect_code) { %>, <%= site.redirect_code === 301 ? 'permanently' : 'temporarily' %>
        (<%= site.redirect_code %>)<% } %>.
    </p>
    <% if (site.redirect_code === 301) { %>
      <div class="tip tip-warn mb-3">
        <span class="tip-ic"></span>
        <div>
          <b>A permanent redirect is remembered by browsers.</b> If you turn this off,
          anyone who already visited may keep going to
          <span class="mono"><%= site.redirect %></span> until they clear their cache.
          Test in a private window.
        </div>
      </div>
    <% } %>
    <form method="post" action="/panel/domains/<%= domain.id %>/redirect">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
      <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" name="action" value="clear" type="submit">
        Turn it off and serve the website again
      </button>
    </form>
  <% } else { %>
    <p class="small muted mb-3">
      Send everyone who visits <b><%= domain.domain %></b> to a different address —
      useful for a second domain you want pointing at your main site, or a name you
      have moved away from.
    </p>

    <form method="post" action="/panel/domains/<%= domain.id %>/redirect">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">

      <div class="field mb-3">
        <label class="label" for="rd-target">Send visitors to</label>
        <input class="input mono" id="rd-target" name="target" placeholder="example.com"
               autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required>
        <p class="hint">
          A domain, or a domain and a page — <code>example.com</code> or
          <code>example.com/welcome</code>. The <code>https://</code> is optional.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="label mb-2">How permanent is this?</p>
      <div class="vers mb-3">
        <label class="ver">
          <input type="radio" name="code" value="301" required>
          <span class="ver-n">Moved for good</span>
          <span class="ver-t">
            301. Search engines move your ranking across, and browsers remember it —
            including if you change your mind. Right for a name you have left behind.
          </span>
        </label>
        <label class="ver">
          <input type="radio" name="code" value="302">
          <span class="ver-n">Just for now</span>
          <span class="ver-t">
            302. Nothing is cached and nothing is transferred, so you can change or
            remove it at any time. Right while you are testing, or for a holding page.
          </span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="tip mb-3">
        <span class="tip-ic"></span>
        <div>
          <b>Not sure? Choose "just for now".</b> You can always make it permanent later,
          and a temporary redirect set by mistake is undone the moment you remove it —
          a permanent one is not.
        </div>
      </div>

      <button class="btn btn-sm" type="submit"><%- icon('arrow', 15) %> Set the redirect</button>
    </form>
  <% } %>
</div>

